WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.204
Hi, I'm Obsidian!

00:00:02.204 --> 00:00:04.033
Not every token needs every layer.

00:00:04.033 --> 00:00:06.775
Here's how a router picks the ones that do.

00:00:08.350 --> 00:00:11.576
Each routed block processes only its top eighth of tokens.

00:00:11.576 --> 00:00:14.157
The rest ride the residual stream past it.

00:00:16.883 --> 00:00:20.204
A router gives each token one number: how much this block wants it.

00:00:20.624 --> 00:00:24.782
Only the top two hundred fifty-six of two thousand and forty-eight get the block.

00:00:25.854 --> 00:00:29.160
Their output is scaled by that number, which trains the router, and

00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:30.261
added to the stream.

00:00:30.681 --> 00:00:34.286
Everyone else skips, carried past on the residual stream for free.

00:00:36.833 --> 00:00:39.823
Each routed block keeps its own eighth, so a token can skip

00:00:39.823 --> 00:00:41.567
a middle block and come back later.

00:00:42.858 --> 00:00:44.549
Two kinds of work shrink differently.

00:00:44.969 --> 00:00:48.496
Projections and the MLP scale with the tokens kept: an eighth.

00:00:48.916 --> 00:00:53.400
Attention scores shrink twice over, fewer queries and fewer keys: a sixty-fourth.

00:00:55.067 --> 00:00:56.863
Top-k needs the whole sequence.

00:00:56.863 --> 00:00:58.660
Sampling only sees the past.

00:00:59.080 --> 00:01:00.262
In training, that's fine.

00:01:02.011 --> 00:01:03.998
So a small predictor learns to guess the cut.

00:01:04.720 --> 00:01:09.702
At sampling time it decides alone, right ninety-seven to ninety-nine percent of the time.

00:01:11.092 --> 00:01:16.446
A small Mixture-of-Depths model matched the baseline's loss and stepped sixty-six percent faster.

00:01:19.525 --> 00:01:23.868
Mixture-of-experts picks among many MLPs, so compute per token stays flat.

00:01:24.288 --> 00:01:28.739
Mixture-of-depths picks one block or nothing, so compute falls, attention included.

00:01:30.017 --> 00:01:33.420
Fix the budget in advance, and the router decides, block by block,

00:01:33.420 --> 00:01:34.555
which tokens spend it.

00:01:37.858 --> 00:01:41.548
A router, a top-k, a residual skip, and a predictor so

00:01:41.548 --> 00:01:42.890
sampling never peeks ahead.

00:01:43.310 --> 00:01:45.533
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:45.533 --> 00:01:46.168
I'm Obsidian.

00:01:46.168 --> 00:01:46.486
Bye!
